  subgraph LAW["⚖️ THE LAW"]
    W1["1. node --check PROVES NOTHING. It passed on a ZERO-BYTE spice.js.<br/><br/>2. A REPORT IS NOT PROOF. LOOK AT THE RENDERED PAGE.<br/>Twist 1: the FILE can be RIGHT and the PAGE still WRONG (tofu note, shadowed).<br/>Twist 2: a RENDER-PROOF CAN PASS AND THE PAGE STILL LEAK — it swept the merged<br/>pool; Health's PRIVATE renderer was never IN the pool.<br/>👉 A PASSING TEST IS A REPORT TOO. Tina found Health in ninety seconds.<br/>👉 PROVE IT PER-SECTION. 'Every room' means EVERY ROOM — 5 of 12 is not proof.<br/>A bad room hides inside a good aggregate.<br/><br/>3. SILENT WRONG IS WORSE THAN LOUD MISSING. A gate that FAILED OPEN. A variable<br/>named 'green' that is ORANGE. Eggs that cost nothing. All reported success.<br/><br/>4. A NARROW QUESTION GETS A NARROW ANSWER — AND IT WILL BE TRUE.<br/>ASK 'WHAT IS NOT GATED?' — NEVER 'is X gated?' Asked the wide way, Code found<br/>kcal ungated in ~8 places, the macro grid in THREE renderers, browse-cost in FIVE<br/>sections. Asked the narrow way, the same model said 'looks fine.'<br/><br/>5. LOCALHOST IS NOT THE LIVE SITE. COMMITTED IS NOT PUSHED. PUSHED IS NOT DEPLOYED.<br/>Check Netlify says PUBLISHED on the hash you think you're testing.<br/><br/>6. DON'T PATCH N SITES. BUILD THE ONE THING THEY SHOULD ALL CALL.<br/>20 isPro wrappers = 20 places to leak again the next time someone adds a room.<br/>3 renderers = one door, one lock. Cost +47 lines. Bought O4 for free.<br/><br/>7. 🆕 AN OVER-GATE IS A BUG TOO. A BLANK IS A BUG. A TEASER IS A PITCH.<br/>The lock is the salesman. If Free sees nothing, you have hidden the price tag<br/>AND the product.<br/><br/>8. 🆕 'SHIP IT' IS NOT 'PUSH IT'. Say which one you mean."]
